[a] run usbterm on the host from the directory inside kcache all the way inside build to where the kernelcache.development.n56 file is

[b] start nanokdp and hit enter to enter iboot

[c] usb get kernelcache.development.n56

[d] bootx ;; this will boot in memory with the kernelcache provided

[e] that's it, now the system is recoverable and you can instal kernelcache using xcrun the usual way
